  "narrative": {
    "essence": "Switzerland is the tournament's most reliable overperformer — they consistently reach knockout rounds despite ranking well below the elite nations. Don't sleep on them. They found their tactical ceiling at the 2022 quarter-final and believe they can go further.",
    "footballIdentity": "Swiss football is a story of multicultural identity. Granit Xhaka, Xherdan Shaqiri, Breel Embolo — born in Kosovo, Nigeria, Cameroon respectively, but raised in Switzerland and fiercely committed to the red and white. The Nati reflects modern Switzerland: a country built on immigration that still debates what belonging means. Their football has become a source of unity in that debate.",
    "theMoment": "Switzerland arrives in 2026 fresh off their deepest World Cup run in decades — a quarter-final in Qatar that proved this isn't just a solid team but a genuine threat. Granit Xhaka, now at Bayer Leverkusen's historic Bundesliga-winning side, is in the form of his life. The squad has depth, tactical maturity, and a manager who found a system that suits them. This is as good as Switzerland gets.",
    "momentType": "footballing"
  },
