  "tactics": {
    "styleTags": [
      "Organized",
      "Counter-attack",
      "High press",
      "Technical"
    ],
    "tacticalNote": "Yakin's 4-2-3-1 is built around defensive solidity and sharp transitions. Xhaka orchestrates from deep, distributing to wide attackers who stretch the game. Switzerland doesn't invite pressure — they press actively and then use the turnover to attack quickly. Their defensive shape concedes very little when it's right.",
    "strength": "Defensive resilience — Switzerland is extremely difficult to score against and has eliminated better teams than themselves through pure tactical discipline.",
    "vulnerability": "Reliance on Xhaka: when he's effectively nullified or unfit, Switzerland's midfield can look pedestrian and their attacks stall."
  },
  "watchFor": [
    "Xhaka's diagonal passes from left midfield — he switches the play with precision that consistently wrong-foots the opposition.",
